                                airport/heliport.</documentation>
                        </annotation>
                    </enumeration>
                    <enumeration value="RWY">
                        <annotation>
                            <documentation>The two aerodromes share all their RWYs and TWYs, but not
                                their aprons.</documentation>
                        </annotation>
                    </enumeration>
                    <enumeration value="PARTIAL">
                        <annotation>
                            <documentation>The two airport/heliports share all their RWYs and TWYs,
                                but not their aprons.</documentation>
                        </annotation>
                    </enumeration>
                    <enumeration value="UNILATERAL">
                        <annotation>
                            <documentation>Unilateral co-location, the RWYs, the TWYs and the aprons
                                of the 1st airport/heliport are available to traffic on the 2nd
                                airport/heliport.</documentation>
                        </annotation>
                    </enumeration>
                    <enumeration value="SEPARATED">
                        <annotation>
                            <documentation>Separated. Even if it is physically possible for an
                                aircraft to taxi between the two airport/heliport manoeuvring areas,
                                this is not operationally allowed.</documentation>
                        </annotation>
                    </enumeration>
